Step 1: Create ASP.NET Core MVC Project
         1. Open Visual Studio 2026.
         2. Click Create a new project.
         3. Select ASP.NET Core Web App (Model-View-Controller).
         4. Project Name: StudentRecordPWA
         5. Framework: .NET 10 or the latest available.
Click Create.
Step 2: Create Student Model
In Solution Explorer, right-click:
Models > Add > Class
Name the file Student.cs.
Write:
namespace StudentRecordPWA.Models
{
     public class Student
     {
          public int Id { get; set; }
          public string Name { get; set; }
          public string Course { get; set; }
          public int Age { get; set; }
     }
}
Step 3: Create Student Controller
         1. Right-click Controllers.
         2. Select Add > Controller.
         3. Choose MVC Controller - Empty.
         4. Name it StudentsController.
Step 4: Write Controller Code
Open StudentsController.cs and write:
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc;
using StudentRecordPWA.Models;
using System.Collections.Generic;
namespace StudentRecordPWA.Controllers
{
     public class StudentsController : Controller
     {
          public IActionResult Index()
          {
              List<Student> students = new List<Student>()
              {
                  new Student
                  {
                       Id = 1,
                       Name = "Rahul",
                       Course = "BSc IT",
                       Age = 20
                  },
                  new Student
                  {
                        Id = 2,
                        Name = "Amit",
                        Course = "BCA",
                        Age = 21
                   },
                   new Student
                   {
                        Id = 3,
                        Name = "Sneha",
                        Course = "BSc CS",
                        Age = 19
                   }
              };
              return View(students);
          }
     }
}
Step 5: Create View Folder
In Solution Explorer, create the following folder:
Views > Students
If the Students folder does not exist, create it inside Views.
Step 6: Create Index View
Right-click Views/Students and select:
         1. Add > View
         2. Choose Razor View - Empty.
         3. Name it Index.cshtml.
Write the following code:
@model IEnumerable<StudentRecordPWA.Models.Student>
<h2>Student Records</h2>
<table border="1" cellpadding="10">
     <tr>
          <th>Id</th>
          <th>Name</th>
          <th>Course</th>
          <th>Age</th>
     </tr>
     @foreach (var item in Model)
     {
          <tr>
            <td>@item.Id</td>
            <td>@item.Name</td>
            <td>@item.Course</td>
            <td>@item.Age</td>
          </tr>
     }
</table>
Step 7: Create Manifest File
Inside wwwroot, create a file named manifest.json.
Write:
{
    "name": "Student Record PWA",
    "short_name": "StudentPWA",
    "start_url": "/Students",
    "display": "standalone",
    "background_color": "#ffffff",
    "theme_color": "#0d6efd",
    "icons": [
        {
            "src": "/icons/icon1.png",
            "sizes": "192x192",
            "type": "image/png"
        },
        {
            "src": "/icons/icon2.png",
            "sizes": "512x512",
            "type": "image/png"
        }
    ]
}
Step 8: Create Icons Folder
            1. Right-click wwwroot.
            2. Select Add > New Folder.
            3. Name it icons.
            4. Add two icon files:
                  o   icon1.png
                  o   icon2.png
Place both files inside the icons folder.
Step 9: Create Service Worker
Inside wwwroot, create a JavaScript file named service-worker.js.
Write:
const CACHE_NAME = "student-pwa-cache";
const urlsToCache = [
     "/Students"
];
self.addEventListener("install", event => {
     event.waitUntil(
          caches.open(CACHE_NAME)
            .then(cache => {
                 return cache.addAll(urlsToCache);
            })
     );
});
self.addEventListener("fetch", event => {
     event.respondWith(
          caches.match(event.request)
            .then(response => {
                 return response || fetch(event.request);
            })
     );
});
Step 10: Register Manifest
Open:
Views > Shared > _Layout.cshtml
Inside the <head> tag, add:
<link rel="manifest" href="/manifest.json">
Step 11: Register Service Worker
In the same _Layout.cshtml file, before the closing </body> tag, add:
<script>
     if ('serviceWorker' in navigator) {
          navigator.serviceWorker.register('/service-worker.js')
            .then(() => console.log('Service Worker Registered'));
     }
</script>
Step 12: Run Application
Append following in Browser URl: /Students
